xgrammar and dlpack (inside libtfgrammar.so)
  https://github.com/mlc-ai/xgrammar (MLC-AI team), https://github.com/dmlc/dlpack (DLPack contributors). Apache License, Version 2.0.
  build.sh copies the prebuilt lib/libtfgrammar.so out of TensorFold's v1.2.7 release archive (aarch64, checked against its
  SHA-256 in profiles.sh) into /opt/tensorfold/native/lib, with the archive's xgrammar and dlpack license and notice files in
  /opt/tensorfold/share/doc/tensorfold/LICENSES-grammar. The library serves structured output and required tool calls; nothing of it is
  modified or compiled here.

PDFium (inside libpdfium.so, PDF document parts)
  https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium (PDFium authors) and https://pypdfium2.readthedocs.io (pypdfium2, pypdfium2
  contributors). BSD-3-Clause, with the licenses of the third-party code the build was made from (freetype, lcms,
  libjpeg-turbo, libpng, agg23, icu, abseil-cpp, fast_float, simdutf, zlib, llvm-libc and others) beside it.
  build.sh downloads the pinned pypdfium2 aarch64 wheel (checked against the SHA-256 in profiles.sh),
  copies pypdfium2_raw/libpdfium.so into /opt/tensorfold/lib (the server loads it through TENSORFOLD_LIBPDFIUM) and the
  wheel's licenses/ tree into /opt/tensorfold/share/doc/tensorfold/LICENSES-pdfium. Nothing of it is modified or
  compiled here, and it is read only when the server runs with --vision --vision-pdf (PDF=1 in profiles.sh).

FFmpeg (linked into libtfvideo.so, video input)
  https://ffmpeg.org/ (the FFmpeg developers). GNU LGPL version 2.1 (this build enables no GPL or version3 component), from the
  release TensorFold pins, 9.0.2, whose source tarball build.sh downloads and checks against the SHA-256 pinned in
  profiles.sh. TensorFold's own tools/zig/build_ffmpeg.sh configures it static and PIC, --disable-programs,
  --disable-shared, --disable-network and --disable-everything with only the H.264, HEVC, VP8, VP9 and MPEG-4 decoders and the
  MP4/MOV and Matroska/WebM demuxers; `zig build video` then links those archives into libtfvideo.so from TensorFold's
  zig/src/video/tf_video.c. The library is installed in /opt/tensorfold/libexec/tfvideo, off the paths the server probes for
  it: only VIDEO=1 puts that directory on the loader's path.
  Nothing of FFmpeg is modified here. FFmpeg's COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and LICENSE.md are in /opt/tensorfold/share/doc/ffmpeg with the
  static archives the link used (/opt/tensorfold/share/doc/ffmpeg/objects, LGPL-2.1 section 3a/6: relinking against a modified
  FFmpeg needs them), and the unmodified FFmpeg source and TensorFold's build script are in the TensorFold checkout's licenses
  and tools/zig/ respectively.

Model files (downloaded from Hugging Face by download.sh; not included in this repository or its image)
  The checkpoint this recipe serves by default, nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local, is NVIDIA's quantization-aware-distilled
  FP4 export (NVIDIA Model Optimizer) of Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next by the Qwen team (Alibaba). Its use is governed by the NVIDIA Open
  Model Agreement (https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-agreement/); the base model is under the
  Qwen Community License 1.0 (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/blob/main/LICENSE).
  The optional overlay (ABLIT=1), drowzeys/keys-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-FP4-QAD-house-qsa-L3-47 by drowzeys, replaces 24
  self_attn.o_proj tensors (weight and scale of 12 layers) of the checkpoint above; it is gated (Responsible Use Agreement) and
  inherits the NVIDIA Open Model License and the Qwen Community License 1.0. download.sh --ablit downloads its sidecar; none of its
  files is part of this repository or its image.
  Upstream's optional INT4 checkpoint, which this recipe does not carry, azampatti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-125B-A5B-INT4-AutoRound, is by azampatti (the
  top-5 expert cut and the shared-expert healing), built on Intel's AutoRound int4 quantization
  (Intel/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-AutoRound) and on Saren-Arterius's hybrid checkpoint and FP8 n-gram table
  (Saren/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-ple-table-fp8), of Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next. Per its model card, it is under the Qwen license
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/blob/main/LICENSE).

